#X obj 673 11 an.onset~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 495 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 An audio onset detector based on the aubio library.
On each detected onset the object sends a bang from the first outlet
and the time of the latest onset in milliseconds from the start of
measurement from the second outlet.;
#X text 240 168 The detection is controlled by @method (one of the
aubio onset detection functions) \, while other properties tune the
analysis: @bs and @hs for the analysis window and hop size \, @threshold
for peak-picking \, @silence for the silence threshold \, @speedlim
for the minimum interval between two consecutive onsets \, @compression
for the lambda logarithmic compression factor \, @awhitening for adaptive
whitening and @delay for compensating a constant system latency.;
#X text 240 314 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 339 • Triggering events on attacks — firing envelopes \,
samples or effects precisely when a note starts \, without any manual
synchronization.;
#X text 250 394 • Beat and rhythm analysis — combining the detector
with tempo estimation tools to identify note onsets in live or recorded
music \, and to drive sequencers \, visualizations or tempo-synced
effects.;
#X text 250 464 • Reactive sound design — using the detected onset
time to trigger short-lived modulations or additional sounds \, so
that the patch reacts to what it hears \, for example in installations
or interactive performances.;
